      "lineNbr": 501,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T17:47:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Device should get rid of its fields holding these gatherers. The push and pop should be part of `drawGeometry()`.  We could extend `AutoResetForDraw` to handle acquiring the gatherers with a pop, and then pushing them back when it goes out of scope.\n\nThat way, we only reach the 2nd level of the stack if we have to record draws for an SkPicture being used as a lazy image or picture shader. Most of the time we will always be pushing/popping the same helper pair for every draw across every device in the Recorder.\n\nIf we push/pop the helper pair when we create the Device, then some devices will hold on to the helpers for quite a long time (if they are part of a client held SkSurface).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 501,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 501,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "5d88755792c78ea334351f0bbaec1d3e39c3a305",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
